"The Demon King was Daran, born to two mages, who found the black filth and made curse power of it."
"Daran's ghost is bound to a small red book of the void, and speaks only to the one who holds it."
"Daran built the Remnant Weapons as living weapons, his children: Straw, Sid, Soma and others."
"Straw is a doll whose soul is one cursed straw; he soaks up despair and spite, and nurtures."
"Sid, the Abhorrent Beast, is a hundred cursed bugs fused in a jar, and lays monster eggs."
"Soma is a golem of filth packed from a hundred Impure Wells, beautiful, idle and deadly."
"Under the world lies black filth: the rotten, mindless intent of some unimaginably vast being."
"The filth is the source of curse power, and seems to be what keeps mages from ascending."
"The world has an authority of gold lines that bars the impossible and recoils from filth."
"Around the world is the void, where many worlds float and vast beings drift."
"Absolutexistence, a being beyond this world's gods, fishes Earth for minds to mend the filth."
"It has cast three before Nala: the Empress, Mirai of the north, and Rhys, who went oversea."
"It seeks people who can reshape the world to their vision, and may cast again if all fail."
"Summons pull from any time on Earth; the two worlds' times do not run together."
"The one it cast before took its question, \"you love trash?\", as his path, and grew mighty."
